# PWM Generator using Verilog

## Description

This project implements a PWM (Pulse Width Modulation) generator
using Verilog HDL.

PWM is commonly used for:

- Motor speed control
- LED brightness control
- Servo control
- Power control

The design uses an 8-bit counter and an 8-bit duty-cycle input.

## Parameters

Counter resolution:

    8 bits

Counter range:

    0 to 255

Duty cycle:

    0% to 100%

## Inputs

    clk        : Clock signal
    reset      : Active-high reset
    duty_cycle : 8-bit duty-cycle control

## Output

    pwm_out    : PWM output signal

## Duty Cycle

    duty_cycle = 0
        PWM = 0%

    duty_cycle = 64
        PWM ≈ 25%

    duty_cycle = 128
        PWM ≈ 50%

    duty_cycle = 192
        PWM ≈ 75%

    duty_cycle = 255
        PWM ≈ 100%

## Operation

An 8-bit counter continuously counts:

    0 -> 1 -> 2 -> ... -> 255 -> 0

PWM output is HIGH when:

    counter < duty_cycle

Otherwise:

    PWM output = LOW

## Files

    pwm_generator.v
        PWM RTL design.

    tb_pwm_generator.v
        Testbench.

    README.md
        Project documentation.

## Simulation

Compile:

    iverilog -o pwm_tb pwm_generator.v tb_pwm_generator.v

Run:

    vvp pwm_tb
